  <h1>CSS: the box<br>model, <em>Flexbox</em><br>&amp; Grid</h1>
  <p class="lede">CSS has a reputation for being fiddly and unpredictable. It isn't — it's a small set of rules applied consistently, and almost all the frustration comes from not knowing three of them: how a box is measured, how the cascade decides who wins, and which layout tool fits which problem. This document is those three things, then Flexbox and Grid properly, then making it work on a phone.</p>

