<div class="cue calm" style="margin-top:24px">
  <p class="cue-k">Read this before anything else</p>
  <p>This assumes you can write HTML and know what the DOM is — CSS selects nodes out of that tree, so if the tree is still fuzzy, go and fix that first.</p>
  <p><strong>CSS is the subject people fake for longest.</strong> It's easy to nudge values until something looks right, ship it, and never find out why it worked. That approach collapses the first time a layout breaks on a screen size you didn't test. The sections on the box model (04–05) and the cascade (03) are the ones that stop that happening.</p>
  <p><strong>There is no time limit and nothing to submit.</strong> Keep a browser open with DevTools next to you the whole way through — CSS is the one topic where reading without looking is close to useless.</p>
</div>

